Hello!

After compiling a xenomai 3.2.1 patched kernel the initramfs can't boot thi=
s kernel because it can't find the root filesystem device.

Error:
Gave up waiting for root file system device. Common problems:
- Boot args (cat /proc/cmdline)
   - Check rootdelay=3D (did the system wait long enough?)
- Missing modules (cat /proc/modules; ls /dev)
ALERT! /dev/mapper/ubuntu-vg-ubuntu-lv does not exist.

When I compile the same kernel sources without xenomai patch it works.

My .config is included and a screenshot of the error as well.
Cat /proc/modules =3D empty
Cat /proc/cmdline =3D BOOT_IMAGE=3D/vmlinuz-5.4.253-xeno-3.2.1 root=3D/dev/=
mapper/ubuntu--vg

I have tried on two systems with different ubuntu versions, kernels and xen=
omai patches.
Ubuntu is installed with LVM but I tried as well without LVM. (Similar erro=
r: UUID does not exist)

# Config FOR UBUNTU 18.04
KERNEL_VERSION=3D"4.19.66"
XENO_VERSION=3D"3.2.1"
XENO_PATCH=3D"ipipe-core-4.19.66-x86-6.patch"

# UBUNTU SRV 20.04
KERNEL_VERSION=3D"5.4.253"
XENO_VERSION=3D"3.2.1"
XENO_PATCH=3D"ipipe-core-5.4.253-x86-14.patch"

Any ideas on what I am doing wrong or how I can debug this problem?

Kind regards,
Max Baeten


